               </item>
               <item>
                <widget class="QLabel" name="secSafetySubtitle">
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>Vital rules for IC pin 1 orientation, polarity standards, electrostatic discharge (ESD), and live testing.</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="wordWrap">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                 <property name="styleSheet">
                  <string>font-size: 13.5px; color: #8ca394;</string>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item>
                <widget class="QFrame" name="s8RulesCard">
                 <property name="role" stdset="0">
                  <string notr="true">card</string>
                 </property>
                 <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="s8RulesCardLayout">
                  <property name="spacing">
                   <number>10</number>
                  </property>
                  <property name="leftMargin">
                   <number>18</number>
                  </property>
                  <property name="topMargin">
                   <number>16</number>
                  </property>
                  <property name="rightMargin">
                   <number>18</number>
                  </property>
                  <property name="bottomMargin">
                   <number>16</number>
                  </property>
                  <item>
                   <widget class="QLabel" name="s8RulesCardTitle">
                    <property name="text">
                     <string>Universal Component Orientation Rules</string>
                    </property>
                    <property name="wordWrap">
                     <bool>true</bool>
                    </property>
                    <property name="styleSheet">
                     <string>font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #00FF85;</string>
                    </property>
                   </widget>
                  </item>
                  <item>
                   <widget class="QLabel" name="s8RulesCardText">
                    <property name="text">
                     <string>1. IC Pin 1 Orientation: When the U-notch points UP, Pin 1 is the top-left pin. When marked with an embossed circular dot, Pin 1 is the pin directly adjacent to the dot. Pin numbering proceeds counter-clockwise around the package.

2. Diode Polarity: Rectifier and signal diodes feature an embossed silver, white, or black band marking the CATHODE (-) terminal. Current flows from Anode (+) to Cathode (-).

3. Electrolytic Capacitor Polarity: The printed stripe with minus signs (---) indicates the NEGATIVE lead. On new through-hole capacitors, the negative lead is also physically shorter. NEVER connect in reverse polarity!

4. Multimeter Resistance &amp; Continuity: ALWAYS disconnect power and discharge all capacitors before probing resistance. Testing an energized circuit can blow the multimeter fuse or damage sensitive semiconductors.</string>
                    </property>
                    <property name="wordWrap">
                     <bool>true</bool>
                    </property>
                    <property name="styleSheet">
                     <string>font-size: 13px;</string>
                    </property>
                   </widget>
                  </item>
                 </layout>
                </widget>
               </item>
